{"id": "EUVD-2021-34888", "enisaUuid": "99fbebe0-7eb4-3603-96f2-fe9015252869", "description": "Vyper from 0.2.13 before 0.2.15 allocates storage slots for @nonreentrant reentrancy locks at the same locations as contract storage variables. When a function using @nonreentrant is called, setting the lock overwrites the overlapping storage variable, corrupting contract state and breaking the contract's intended logic.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:36:18", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vyperlang/vyper/security/advisories/GHSA-7f92-rr6w-cq64", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vyper-0.2.13-before-0.2.15-storage-corruption-via-nonreentrant-decorator"], "aliases": ["CVE-2021-48018", "GHSA-57w3-rr8j-wp9c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ea2853da-9362-3172-886b-7f535f042a62", "product": {"name": "vyper", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}, "product_version": "0.2.13 <0.2.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "117274db-a96b-3df8-8589-b3f297534e21", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}], "isExploited": false}